## Decisions

- d1 `packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive-mode.ts` InteractiveMode.init — composer.setRuntimeChildren([...]) retained-mode runtime children list (around line 2644): **combined**. L60.2 requires that a widget set with placement "hud" renders into hookWidgetContainerHud, and that this container sits with the pinned HUD rows above the editor in fullscreen mode and in the transcript region otherwise. The fork (L) introduced hookWidgetContainerHud in 173d7abe54 and mounted it in the retained-mode transcript region right after todoContainer and before subagentContainer (transcriptRegion.addChild(this.hookWidgetContainerHud)), and as a fullscreen layout beforeEditor row. Upstream (R) has no such container; it refactored the retained-mode mount into composer.setRuntimeChildren([...]). The merge kept the fullscreen beforeEditor row and the fullscreen `borrowed` detach list but dropped the retained-mode mount, so in retained mode the hud widget was never mounted anywhere. The fix re-adds the container to the upstream runtime-children list at the fork's original position (after todoContainer, before subagentContainer), which is also where the fullscreen beforeEditor list places it. Nothing else changes: the fullscreen path still borrows and detaches the container from the TUI and paints it via FullscreenChatLayout.beforeEditor, and the container stays unclassified in transientChrome/selfClearingChrome/billedChrome exactly like its sibling hookWidgetContainerAbove, so the post-run chrome floor behaves as before.
- d2 `packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive-mode.ts` InteractiveMode.init — composer.setRuntimeChildren([...]) retained-mode runtime children list (line 2645): **combined**. L60.2 requires that a widget set with placement "hud" renders into hookWidgetContainerHud, and that this container sits with the pinned HUD rows above the editor in fullscreen mode and in the transcript region otherwise. The fork (L) introduced hookWidgetContainerHud in 173d7abe54 and mounted it in the retained-mode transcript region right after todoContainer and before subagentContainer (transcriptRegion.addChild(this.hookWidgetContainerHud)), and as a fullscreen layout beforeEditor row. Upstream (R) has no such container; it refactored the retained-mode mount into composer.setRuntimeChildren([...]). The merge kept the fullscreen beforeEditor row and the fullscreen `borrowed` detach list but dropped the retained-mode mount, so in retained mode the hud widget was never mounted anywhere. The fix re-adds the container to the upstream runtime-children list at the fork's original position (after todoContainer, before subagentContainer), which is also where the fullscreen beforeEditor list places it. Nothing else changes: the fullscreen path still borrows and detaches the container from the TUI and paints it via FullscreenChatLayout.beforeEditor, and the container stays unclassified in transientChrome/selfClearingChrome/billedChrome exactly like its sibling hookWidgetContainerAbove, so the post-run chrome floor behaves as before.

